---
/**
 * t59 · Plain Carrier
 *
 * The message shape everyone already reads, drawn properly: the bottom-left
 * corner is spent on the tail instead of a second radius, so the bottom edge
 * runs unbroken and the tail is the left edge continuing rather than a wedge
 * stuck on.
 *
 * The tail is the lower-left corner rather than an addition to it: the left
 * edge runs straight past the bottom edge and rakes back up to it over 3
 * rows, taper 7-4-2. Because that corner is never rounded the bottom edge
 * stays 24 pixels unbroken, and that edge is what still reads as a message
 * at 16px, where the tail itself is barely a pixel and a half.
 *
 * Radius 7 on the three corners that survive. The face sits high of centre
 * by a row, because the tail already weights the mark downward and splitting
 * the difference would read as sagging.
 *
 * 7 tones peel inward as contour rings, one step per ring, so every band
 * bends around the corners and around the tail — Hozz's meniscus rather than
 * a rectangle dropped inside an outline. The direction is Mozz's, but spent
 * on where the bands sit instead of on extra tones: a pixel's effective
 * depth is pushed inward by up to 1.5 rings on the side facing away from the
 * light, so the meniscus is wide on the lit shoulder and the deep field
 * rises nearly to the keyline on the far one. The keyline carries it too —
 * two key tones, the lit part of the rim taking the lighter.
 *
 * Spending the direction that way is what keeps the middle calm. The field
 * is one flat tone, 156 pixels of it, and no two touching pixels anywhere in
 * the mark are more than one tone apart.
 *
 * The face is supplied and untouched — facePathsAt at md with the compact
 * smile and the family gap of 2, which is exactly 8×8 — centred on the body
 * with the tail ignored: 8 rows of air above and 7 below, measured. Nothing
 * is cleared for it; white on the field is 7.6:1.
 *
 * 10 tones.
 */
import MarkFrame from '../MarkFrame.astro';
import { facePathsAt } from '../../../data/mark';

interface Props { size?: number }
const { size = 128 } = Astro.props;
---

<MarkFrame size={size} title="Twozz — Plain Carrier">
